{"name":"Black Sable","hex":"#434b4d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"black","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Absorbing all light and reflecting none; dark and hueless.","Without light."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour/color perceived in the absence of light, but also when no light is reflected, but rather absorbed.","A black dye or pigment."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/black"},{"term":"sable","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small carnivorous mammal of the Old World that resembles a weasel, Martes zibellina, from cold regions in Eurasia and the North Pacific islands, valued for its dark brown fur.","Any other marten, especially Martes americana (syn. Mustela americana)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Sable-coloured, black.","In blazon, of the colour black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sable"}],"entries":[{"title":"European polecat","blocks":[{"text":"The European polecat, also known as the western polecat, is a mustelid species occurring in Europe and the Rif mountains. It is of a generally dark brown colour, with a pale underbelly and a dark mask across the face. Occasionally, colour mutations including albinos, leucists, isabellinists, xanthochromists, amelanists, and erythrists occur. It has a shorter, more compact body than other Mustela species, a more powerfully built skull and dentition, is less agile, and is well known for having the characteristic ability to secrete a particularly foul-smelling liquid to mark its territory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Storm_the_polecat.jpg/330px-Storm_the_polecat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_polecat","wikidata":"Q26582"},{"title":"Sable","blocks":[{"text":"The sable is a species of marten, a small omnivorous mammal primarily inhabiting the forest environments of Russia, from the Ural Mountains throughout Siberia, and northern Mongolia. Its habitat also borders eastern Kazakhstan, China, North Korea, and Hokkaido, Japan."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Sobol_bur.jpg/330px-Sobol_bur.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable","wikidata":"Q26423"},{"title":"Black","blocks":[{"text":"Black is a color that results from the absence or complete absorption of visible light. It is an achromatic color, without chroma, like white and grey. It is often used symbolically or figuratively to represent darkness. Black and white have often been used to describe opposites such as good and evil, the Dark Ages versus the Age of Enlightenment, and night versus day. Since the Middle Ages, black has been the symbolic color of solemnity and authority, and for this reason it is still commonly worn by judges and magistrates."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png/330px-Tutankhamun_jackal_%28blacked%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black","wikidata":"Q23445"},{"title":"Sable (tincture)","blocks":[{"text":"In heraldry, sable is the tincture equivalent to black. It is one of the five dark tinctures called colours."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sable_(tincture)","wikidata":"Q936496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Chaucer_Polcat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/45/Chaucer_Polcat.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Polcat, as it appears in The Pardoner's Tale from the Ellesmere Chaucer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChaucer_Polcat.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia